# Conventions

## Context

`app/` is strict TypeScript (`noUncheckedIndexedAccess` on) with a few fixed
style rules that keep the codebase consistent.

## Rule

- Named exports only, no `any`, no `@ts-ignore`.
- Update state immutably (spread/`map`/`filter`), never mutate it in place
  (no `push`, `splice`, or direct property assignment on state).
- Filenames kebab-case; types/interfaces PascalCase.

## How to verify

1. `cd app && npm run typecheck` passes.
2. `grep -rn "export default" app/src` → no matches.
3. `grep -rnE "\bany\b|@ts-ignore" app/src` → no matches (typecheck alone
   won't catch these since explicit `any` and `@ts-ignore` still compile).
